# The devshell, applied to the current shell rather than a nested one.
#
# `nix develop` spawns its own bash and sets SHELL to it, and lunette hands its
# environment to every client it spawns, so a terminal started from a session
# run that way comes up on a shell from the store with none of the user's setup.
# direnv exports the same environment into the shell that is already running,
# which leaves SHELL alone.
#
# Run `direnv allow` once. `docs/dev/build-and-development.md` has the rest.
use flake
